top', 'sub-par', 'Service-check', 'in-house', 'been-stepped-in-and-tracked-everywhere', 'multi-grain', 'to-go', 'non-customer', 'High-quality', 'sit-down', 'over-whelm', 'low-key', 'non-fancy', 'golden-crispy', 'over-priced', 'over-hip', 'under-services']\n"]}]},{"cell_type":"code","source":[],"metadata":{"id":"SgzIL74ZMtGw"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["*   **Pregunta 12.**  \n","\n","Busca e imprime todas las palabras que terminan con la conjugación en inglés \"ing\" o \"ed\".\n","\n","No deben importar mayúsculas o minúsculas.\n","\n","Indica la cantidad de palabras que encontraste de cada una."],"metadata":{"id":"DEIgl79HMthr"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["res12_ing = [re.findall(r'\\b\\w+ing\\b', d, re.I) for d in docs_clean]\n","res12_ed = [re.findall(r'\\b\\w+ed\\b', d, re.I) for d in docs_clean]\n","\n","flat_ing = [item for sublist in res12_ing for item in sublist]\n","flat_ed = [item for sublist in res12_ed for item in sublist]\n","\n","print(f\"Palabras en 'ing': {len(flat_ing)}\")\n","print(f\"Palabras en 'ed': {len(flat_ed)}\")"],"metadata":{"id":"I4TSofBMMv9y","colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1777944637654,"user_tz":360,"elapsed":22,"user":{"displayName":"luis gallegos","userId":"03125789092232740572"}},"outputId":"8677e933-51c0-418d-98ce-3345a1654a9b"},"execution_count":21,"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["Palabras en 'ing': 280\n","Palabras en 'ed': 339\n"]}]},{"cell_type":"code","source":[],"metadata":{"id":"AhGq6De2Mvyh"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["#**Parte 3. Proceso de limpieza.**"],"metadata":{"id":"70StdqAZa9E9"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["*   **Pregunta 13.**  \n","\n","Ahora realiza un proceso de limpieza del corpus que incluya los siguientes procesos:\n","\n","*   Solo se deben considerar caracteres alfabéticos, incluyendo algún tipo de acentuación. Es decir, se eliminan todos los signos de puntuación y caracteres especiales.\n","*   Todos los caracteres alfabéticos se transforman a minúsculas.\n","*   Se deben eliminar todos los espacios en blanco adicionales que se puedan encontrar en cada comentario.\n","\n","Al finalizar dicho proceso de limpieza, imprime el resultado de los primeros 10 comentarios resultantes.\n","   \n","\n","\n"],"metadata":{"id":"xaDUFXHrMvX2"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["def limpiar_texto(texto):\n","    # 1. Solo alfabéticos y espacios (manteniendo acentos)\n","    texto = re.sub(r'[^a-zA-ZáéíóúÁÉÍÓÚ\\s]', '', texto)\n","    # 2. Minúsculas\n","    texto = texto.lower()\n","    # 3. Eliminar espacios extra\n","    texto = re.sub(r'\\s+', ' ', texto).strip()\n","    return texto\n","\n","corpus_limpio = [limpiar_texto(d) for d in docs_clean]\n","\n","print(\"Primeros 10 comentarios tras limpieza profunda:\")\n","for d in corpus_limpio[:10]:\n","    print(f\"- {d}\")"],"metadata":{"id":"K3kQzPOPMx0w","colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1777944651923,"user_tz":360,"elapsed":46,"user":{"displayName":"luis gallegos","userId":"03125789092232740572"}},"outputId":"b67a3176-babc-44cd-b0ff-e55a2cca8fbf"},"execution_count":22,"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["Primeros 10 comentarios tras limpieza profunda:\n","- wow loved this place\n","- crust is not good\n","- not tasty and the texture was just nasty\n","- stopped by during the late may bank holiday off rick steve recommendation and loved it\n","- the selection on the menu was great and so were the prices\n","- now i am getting angry and i want my damn pho\n","- honeslty it didnt taste that fresh\n","- the potatoes were like rubber and you could tell they had been made up ahead of time being kept under a warmer\n","- the fries were great too\n","- a great touch\n"]}]},{"cell_type":"code","source":[],"metadata":{"id":"mYEDlHSFMyJN"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["*   **Pregunta 14.**  \n","\n","Supongamos que en un primer análisis básico consideramos como nuestro nuevo corpus el texto obtenido después del proceso de limpieza del ejercicio anterior.  \n","\n","A partir de este nuevo corpus consideraremos cada palabra (cadena de caracteres) resultante como los \"tokens\" de nuestro estudio.\n","\n","Y a partir de este documento tokenizado generamos nuestro diccionario de tokens.\n","\n","¿Cuántos tokens diferentes tiene nuestro diccionario?\n"],"metadata":{"id":"WZwEhg2lUSAX"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["# Tokenizamos por espacio\n","todas_las_palabras = \" \".join(corpus_limpio).split()\n","vocabulario = set(todas_las_palabras)\n","\n","print(f\"Número total de tokens: {len(todas_las_palabras)}\")\n","print(f\"Número de tokens únicos (diccionario): {len(vocabulario)}\")"],"metadata":{"id":"kbAL9-v0V-jx","colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1777944659293,"user_tz":360,"elapsed":10,"user":{"displayName":"luis gallegos","userId":"03125789092232740572"}},"outputId":"67384356-bf52-4692-e12c-8319405ed07d"},"execution_count":23,"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["Número total de tokens: 10777\n","Número de tokens únicos (diccionario): 2051\n"]}]},{"cell_type":"code","source":[],"metadata":{"id":"DZs_etmiV-fd"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["*   **Pregunta 15.**  \n","\n","Finalmente, en este ejercicio definiremos nuestro conjunto de palabras denominado \"stopwords\", es decir, las palabras (cadenas de caracteres) que tienen frecuencias muy altas, pero que no aportan mucho valor para el significado/entendimiento de cada comentario.\n","\n","Recuerda que ejemplos de stopwords son artículos, adverbios, conectivos, etcétera.\n","\n","* **15a.** Con base a la lista de stopwords que se te proporciona, realiza un proceso de limpieza eliminando todas estas palabras del corpus obtenido en el